15 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting EEG signal processing for emotion classification. Left: EEG data from a head is converted into graphs with nodes and edges. Middle: Nodes processed through Leaky ReLU and DGAT Modules. Right: Resulting data represented in clusters and emoticons indicating emotional states like happy, neutral, and sad. Labels DEAP and SEED indicate datasets or frameworks used.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a three-session experiment involving emotional film clips and EEG monitoring. Clips labeled as happy, sad, neutral, and fear. Sessions consist of trials one through fifteen. Each trial includes a start hint, film clip, self-assessment, and rest phase. Brain activity is recorded and displayed on a monitor.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating self-attention in neural networks. On the left, inputs \\\(\\vec{h_i}\\\) and \\\(\\vec{h_j}\\\) are transformed by \\\(W\\\) weights and aggregated by function \\\(\\vec{a}\\\). The right shows nodes \\\(\\vec{h_1}\\\) to \\\(\\vec{h_6}\\\), with attention scores \\\(\\alpha_{ij}\\\). The outputs are concatenated and linked to \\\(\\vec{h'_1}\\\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Diagram of two electrode positions for EEG, labeled \215SEED\216 and \215DEAP.\216 The SEED configuration includes rows of electrodes such as FP, F, C, P, and O, with 62 positions. The DEAP configuration features fewer electrodes with a similar naming pattern, totaling 32 positions. Both diagrams are top-view representations of a head, marked with circular notes corresponding to electrode positions, indicative of different setups for EEG studies.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a graph neural network model. Node features and a brain graph form the input graph. The DGAT module applies multihead attention and concatenation, followed by Leaky ReLU activation. The pooling layer leads to full connection, applying Softmax for classification, depicting faces with different emotions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing accuracy percentages for fifteen subjects. Most subjects have accuracy between 90 and 100 percent, with a slight dip around 80 percent for some subjects. The y-axis represents accuracy in percent, and the x-axis lists subjects from one to fifteen.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing accuracy percentages for 32 subjects, comparing arousal and valence. Both categories are represented by different colors: arousal in blue and valence in orange. Accuracy ranges from 65% to 100%.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Scatter plots comparing DEAP and DEAP-DGAT data. The left plot shows a positive linear correlation between blue and orange points in a diagonal orientation. The right plot shows blue points clustered vertically and orange points clustered separately on the right.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Three confusion matrices for emotion recognition: The top left shows DEAP Valence with high accuracy \(91.95% negative, 94.12% positive\). The top right shows DEAP Arousal with similar accuracy \(91.94% negative, 94.67% positive\). The bottom matrix shows SEED data with three labels \(negative, neutral, positive\), emphasizing accuracy in neutral detections \(95.08%\). Color gradient indicates the scale from zero to one.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Three circular diagrams labeled Positive, Neutral, and Negative, show relationships among various colored segments, each marked with labels like AF3, Fp1, and CP5. Red lines connect the segments, indicating connections or interactions. Each circle's segments are differently colored, ranging from red to blue, with similar patterns of red lines across diagrams, though varying in density and distribution.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Three contour maps showing brain activity in red and yellow shades. The left map is labeled \215Positive,\216 the middle \215Neutral,\216 and the right \215Negative.\216 Darker regions indicated higher activity levels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Bar graph compares accuracy percentages for DGAT, MA-GAT, and GAT across two categories, Valence and Arousal. DGAT shows highest accuracy, followed by MA-GAT, then GAT, for both categories.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
